# --- Wave B1 shape-drain: tagging cardinality + suppression ---
# gmeow:TaggingHasPlayersShape — a Tagging tags exactly one entity with exactly one tag and one tagger.
gmeow:Tagging logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:taggingTagged ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:taggingTag ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:taggingTagger ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects OWL FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.

gmeow:taggingSchemeFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/tags> ;
    rdfs:label "taggingScheme is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:taggingScheme is functional: a gmeow:Tagging act is performed within exactly one scheme — even though the applied tag may itself be cross-listed in several schemes via gmeow:tagInScheme, the act names a single scheme context. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:taggingScheme ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:taggingScheme ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:taggingScheme names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:taggingScheme, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:taggingScheme and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:taggingScheme (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:taggingSchemeFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:taggingScheme ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
